('Jeep','North America','1941-present','Automotive and outdoor goods',"In the style of Jeep, rugged, utilitarian, honest, military-derived adventure design. Flat, boxy, squared-off forms with short overhangs and strong right angles. Olive drab, sand, desert tan, safety yellow and bright orange, used flat and matte. Exposed bolts and fixings, heavy black matte plastic or rubber edging, chunky knobby textures and bare painted metal. Simple repeated vertical rhythm and round accents. Hose-down simplicity, function first, ready for mud, sand and weather, in any category from tools to clothing to timepieces."),
('MG','Europe','1924-present','Automotive',"In the style of MG, small, jaunty, open sporting spirit in a British 1930s to 1960s mood. Compact, low, cheerful proportions with separate sweeping curves, rounded ends and bright polished chrome rims against enamel. Racing green, red, cream, ivory and pale blue. Red or black leather, engine-turned metal and warm wooden panels. A repeated octagon motif and fine vertical lines. Spirited, plucky and simple, with period charm."),
